{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>The Rock, His work is perfect.</b> Even though He is strong, when He brings punishment upon those who transgress His will, He does not bring it as a flood but in justice — for <b>His work is perfect</b>." "<b>A El of faithfulness.</b> To pay the righteous their due in the World to Come — and even though He delays their reward, in the end He confirms His words." "<b>And without injustice.</b> Even to the wicked He pays the reward of their righteousness in this world (cf. Sifrei)." "<b>Righteous and upright is He.</b> All vindicate His judgment upon themselves, and so it is fitting and upright for them — <b>righteous</b> from the mouth of mankind, <b>and upright is He</b> and fitting to be vindicated."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:08.073318999Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}